    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside profiles of **Jackson Merrill** (74.60) and **Gunnar Henderson** (67.48). **Jackson Merrill** is our primary target against Holmes, benefiting from a massive 13% boost due to dynamic platoon positioning and a favorable matchup against a 4.47 xERA starter. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** (65.57) are poised to feast on Aldegheri\u2019s 5.75 xERA; despite a platoon penalty for **Gunnar Henderson**, his elite base projection and the soft matchup keep him as a top-tier play. We are also monitoring **Andy Pages**, who earns a 62.80 score thanks to a rare confluence of favorable park factors and the tendency of opposing pitcher Matthews to work at a pace that creates high-efficiency stolen base opportunities\u2014a critical edge given our internal weight on SB scarcity.\n\nOur most difficult lineup management decision centered on the bench, where **Miguel Vargas** (47.86) and **Nolan Schanuel** (47.80) both finished just shy of the starting threshold. **Miguel Vargas** remains the most intriguing \"next man up,\" but he was ultimately relegated to the bench because his projection is heavily hampered by a matchup against Williams, whose ability to limit baserunners directly devalues **Miguel Vargas**\u2019s specific utility profile. Similarly, **Nasim Nunez** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** were evaluated but kept below the 40-point floor due to the combination of sub-optimal batting orders and facing Mayza, whose profile as an elite situational pitcher makes him a difficult target for our speed-first specialists. We are proceeding with **Wade Meckler** in the final OF slot; although his 40.42 score is marginal, his current lineup placement and the projected game flow provide enough upside to maintain his roster spot over the available bench alternatives.",
